"With the help of Britain's government, donors, national governments and global nationals just like you, we can make malnutrition's social injustice become just a footnote in the book of history," Tracey Ullman, Ambassador of The Power of Nutrition, told the crowd during a live concert in London in April 2018.
After more than 5,000 actions were carried out in the U.K
Responsiding to one of the most common questions on their website: "What makes you think you can eliminate extreme poverty?"
Global Citizen replied: "It's going to be a lousy and difficult road, we'll sometimes fall off and fail.
However, such as the great civil or anti-apartheid rights movements that took place before us, we will succeed, because together we are stronger.
